This folder contains scripts related to Section 5 of the manuscript, which 
estimates the effects of smoke at parks on nearby spending.

The contents, in order, are:

"01_safegraph_api_call.R": this script downloads all Safegraph Spend data from Dewey
"02_safegraph_weekly_placekey_filter.R": this script reads in Safegraph data and processes the dataset at a weekly resolution
"03_safegraph_weekly_covariates_process.R": this script reads in the processed Safegraph data and generates all weather, smoke, pm2.5, etc. data at the weekly level
"04_safegraph_final_weekly_data_process.R": this script reads in the processed Safegraph data and creates all final variables
"05_advan_poi_filter.R": this script takes the raw advan data and filters it to just include points of interest around parks
"06_advan_daily_covariates_process.R": this script takes POI points and attributes all rasterized pollution, weather, smoke_plume, and fire distance data to the given POIs. It also adds in daily park-level covariates
"07_safegraph_daily_data_process.R": this script takes monthly-level Safegraph spending data, converts to daily, and combines with daily visitation data and other relevant covariates
"08_regressions_safegraph.R": this script runs spending-related regressions using daily data
"09_regressions_weekly_safegraph.R": this script creates a weekly-level version of the daily spending dataset and estimates weekly-level regressions as a robustness check on credit/debit report timing inconsistencies
"10_create_gateway_com_map.R": This script creates maps of parks and their associate gateway communities for inclusion as supplementary information in the appendix.


